          ],
          "content": "Also, write down the steps you followed to draw the angle."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.488,
            0.756,
            0.515
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "2.11 Types of Angles and their Measures"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.528,
            0.885,
            0.62
          ],
          "content": "We have read about different types of angles in this chapter. We have seen that a straight angle is $1 8 0 ^ { \\circ }$ and a right angle is $9 0 ^ { \\circ }$ . How can other types of angles — acute and obtuse — be described in terms of their degree measures?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.628,
            0.884,
            0.673
          ],
          "content": "**Acute Angle:** Angles that are smaller than the right angle, i.e., less than $9 0 ^ { \\circ }$ and are greater than $0 ^ { \\circ } ,$ , are called **acute** angles."
        },
